  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive at full health when the planner stopped. Decisions 3907-3908 selected disintegration and targeted the DM-100; accepted transition 3908 records one turn, six experience, consumption of the public magic boost and disappearance of the enemy. Decision 3909 then rejected progress because a separate lightning-lane memory survived. The displayed defeat message was stale, and the existing missile-only receipt did not cover this attack. Public Arcane Vision provides a narrower supported correction: an enemy successfully struck by this guaranteed-hit beam would remain tracked if alive. The proposed receipt requires that talent, a publicly established beam range, a consumed non-expiring boost, matching attack memory and corroborating experience. Original policy fails two new regression assertions; the candidate passes all three tests. The full suite passes 1910 tests with four skips. An isolated probe using the recorded public targeting inputs reproduces the original gate and removes it on the candidate. This does not establish a safe next movement or subsequent survival.",
    "learnings": "Keep remembered lightning threats separate from ordinary sightings, but retire matching memory when a rigorously confirmed tracked attack proves that caster cannot remain alive. Experience and disappearance alone are insufficient for a penetrating beam; preserve threat memory when tracking, range or successful execution is uncertain."
  },
